# The root expression of this caos client repo: mount caos' `std/` as THIS
# directory's evaluation result, so everything below can name `caos-std/<entry>`.
#
# This directory holds the whole pin -- this expression, flake.nix and
# flake.lock -- and nothing else, which is the point. The loader is run over
# `--in:@=.`, and a tree's expression is cached on that tree. At the repo root
# that tree is the whole session and changes with every tool call, so the loader
# re-ran, as a worker job, before every lookup. Here its input is three files
# that do not change while the session does, so it is answered from cache.
# `--output-path=.` replaces this directory with std; the loader still reads
# flake.nix and flake.lock from `--in` to check the pin first.
#
# Nothing of caos is committed here. The mount exists only in the evaluated
# tree -- content-addressed, deduped, never on disk.
#
# ONE LINE, and it has to be: a directive is a line, and there are no backslash
# continuations. design/flake-inputs.md wraps this same expression across four
# lines to fit the page; copying that wrapping verbatim makes every resolution
# of `caos-std/` fail.
#
# The locator appears TWICE on purpose (design/flake-inputs.md, "Consumer
# root"): `--base` yields the loader's own image, `--input-tree` yields the
# tree it splices. Passing the tree as an argument is what lets the server's
# `:@@=` resolution fetch it before the request is keyed, so the ArgTree
# carries an oid and the URL never enters a cache key.
#
# Both revs must equal what flake.lock locks for `--input=caos`. The loader
# checks exactly that and refuses the evaluation if they differ.
run --base:@@=github:softmax-universe/caos?rev=2f3de65669b5c8834e4136047b221807a6392027&dir=std/flake-input-loader --in:@=. --expr=$CAOS_EXPR --input=caos --input-tree:@@=github:softmax-universe/caos?rev=2f3de65669b5c8834e4136047b221807a6392027&dir=std --output-path=.
